Short:        Run jobs on extra CPU cores, open spec
Uploader:     (Dale fills this in at upload time)
Author:       Dale Kirkwood (Dalsin Limited)
Type:         util/libs
Version:      0.1
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Distribution: Aminet

OpenMulticore is an open specification for presenting extra processor cores to
AmigaOS, and openmulticore.library, which programs open to run work on them.
The motherboard CPU keeps Exec and the custom chips; extra cores run jobs in
shared memory and hand anything the OS must do back to it.

Cores come from an autoconfig board with a published register map (a doorbell,
a latch that stops the cores while a game takes the machine, job and
completion rings in Fast RAM) or from a software provider, for cores that are
not on the Zorro bus, such as a PiStorm's spare Raspberry Pi cores. Anyone may
build hardware or a provider to the specification.

The library gives programs the cores, memory grants every core may use, jobs
with completion signals, a one-call way to run a 68k function on another core,
and batches of maths. powerpc.library and ppc.library (WarpOS and PowerUP) can
sit on top as faces when a PowerPC core exists.

Status: this archive is the specification. The library and AmigaChrome's board
follow; AmigaChrome (an Amiga for the PC) implements it first with cores that
run on the host.

